content="```yml\n---\n- name: Install EPEL on compatible systems\n  become: yes\n  when: ansible_distribution in ['Amazon', 'RedHat'] or ansible_distribution_major_version in ['7', '8', '9', '10']\n\n  tasks:\n  - name: Add the EPEL GPG key\n    rpm_key:\n      state: present\n      key: 'https://dl.fedoraproject.org/lp/people/paul/howdy/RPM-GPG-KEY-EPEL-10'\n\n  - name: Install the EPEL-release package\n    yum:\n      name: epel-release\n      state: present\n      update_cache: yes\n\n  - name: Install the EPEL-next-release package (optional)\n    yum:\n      name: epel-next-release\n      state: present\n      update_cache: yes\n    when: epel_next | bool\n\n  - name: Update package cache\n    package:\n      name: '*'\n      state: present\n      update_cache: yes\n    when: epel_next | bool\n```\nNote: The above playbook assumes you have the `epel_next` variable defined somewhere in your playbook or inventory. If not, you can define it as a variable in your playbook or inventory file. \n\nAlso, ensure you have the `yum` package installed on your system, and the `epel-release` and `epel-next-release` packages are available in the specified repositories. \n\nPlease ensure you have the `become` enabled for the playbook to run as a privileged user." additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'llama3.1:8b', 'created_at': '2025-10-20T06:38:16.104991298Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 2870573792, 'load_duration': 121669695, 'prompt_eval_count': 512, 'prompt_eval_duration': 33199211, 'eval_count': 325, 'eval_duration': 2713695824, 'model_name': 'llama3.1:8b'} id='run--425cce7a-1bec-4cbe-90b7-8cea5d0f561e-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 512, 'output_tokens': 325, 'total_tokens': 837}
